{"step_index":255,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T00:52:25Z","input_tokens":10641,"cache_read_tokens":80371,"output_tokens":788,"thinking":"I'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\nInitial diagnostic map visualization should include a base layer of continental provinces/cantons in light gray with white thin borders. Event data will be overlaid as red, transparent points, adjusting size to avoid overlap. The final figure should have a formal title, legend, and high resolution. It's essential to examine the coordinate ranges of the georeferenced data before setting axis limits for the map. I'll check the minimum and maximum latitude/longitude in the georeferenced data versus the bounding box of the canton map to identify any potential coordinate range issues before generating the diagnostic map.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"Set-Location D:\\\\Tesis; .\\\\.venv\\\\Scripts\\\\python.exe -c \\\"\\nimport pandas as pd\\nfrom src.validacion_geo.cartografia import cargar_mapa_cantonal\\ndf = pd.read_parquet('data/processed/homi_georreferenciado.parquet')\\nmapa = cargar_mapa_cantonal()\\nprint('Map bounds (minx, miny, maxx, maxy):', mapa.total_bounds)\\nprint('Points lon min/max:', df['lon_num'].min(), df['lon_num'].max())\\nprint('Points lat min/max:', df['lat_num'].min(), df['lat_num'].max())\\nminx, miny, maxx, maxy = mapa.total_bounds\\nout = df[(df['lon_num'] < minx - 0.5) | (df['lon_num'] > maxx + 0.5) | (df['lat_num'] < miny - 0.5) | (df['lat_num'] > maxy + 0.5)]\\nprint('Points outside map bbox +-0.5 deg:', len(out))\\nif len(out) > 0:\\n    print(out[['provincia', 'canton', 'lat_num', 'lon_num']].head(10))\\n\\\"\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"10000","toolSummary":"\"Check map bounds vs event coordinate bounds\""}}]}
