{"step_index":257,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T00:52:44Z","input_tokens":3259,"cache_read_tokens":88963,"output_tokens":6228,"thinking":"Map boundaries and point coordinates are almost perfectly aligned. The map bounds encompass the point data, suggesting the issue isn't a simple coordinate mismatch. This empirical check strongly suggests data alignment is correct, shifting the focus to another cause.\n\n\nEvery point is correctly within Ecuador's continental boundaries. The initial concern about outliers can be disregarded; the \"limbo\" points are boundary discrepancies, not ocean errors.\n\nThe `mapa` data has the `DPA_DESPRO` field, so dissolving the cantonal polygons by `DPA_DESPRO` creates a provincial outline for overlay. This provides a base cantonal layer, a provincial boundary overlay, and an events layer with micro-jitter for visualization.\n\n\nA micro-jitter effect has been applied to event points to prevent overlapping at identical coordinates, mirroring a visualization technique for clarity. Empty space in the southeastern region of the map offers an ideal location for the legend, which should be verified visually. This approach avoids obscuring any relevant data clusters or cantonal boundaries.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"# Paquete `visualizacion` — Fase 5.6: cartografía diagnóstica de validación para tesis.\\n\"","Overwrite":"true","Path":"\"D:\\\\Tesis\\\\src\\\\visualizacion\\\\__init__.py\""}},{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"\"r\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nmapa_diagnostico.py — Generación del mapa diagnóstico de validación continental (Paso 5.6).\\n\\nCorresponde a la Fase R 12 (líneas 522-557) del script original:\\n    Mapa_Provincias <- Mapa_Completo %>%\\n      filter(DPA_DESPRO != \\\"GALAPAGOS\\\") %>%\\n      group_by(DPA_DESPRO) %>%\\n      summarize(.groups = \\\"drop\\\")\\n\\n    ggplot() +\\n      geom_sf(data = Mapa_Provincias, fill = \\\"gray96\\\", color = \\\"black\\\", size = 0.4) +\\n      geom_jitter(data = test_mapa, aes(geometry = geometry),\\n                  stat = \\\"sf_coordinates\\\", alpha = 0.4, color = \\\"darkred\\\", size = 0.8) +\\n      theme_minimal() +\\n      labs(title = \\\"Distribución Geográfica de Homicidios en Ecuador\\\", ...)\\n\\nObjetivo en Python (Paso 5.6):\\n    Generar de forma 100% desatendida (sin abrir ventanas emergentes que bloqueen la\\n    consola) una figura cartográfica en alta resolución (`dpi=300`) lista para tesis:\\n      • Capa base cantonal: polígonos continentales en gris neutro claro (`#E0E0E0`)\\n        con bordes internos blancos delgados (`edgecolor=\\\"white\\\"`).\\n      • Capa de referencia provincial: contornos provinciales disueltos (`dissolve`)\\n        en gris grafito suave para facilitar la lectura territorial.\\n      • Capa de eventos: puntos georreferenciados en rojo carmesí con transparencia\\n        controlada (`alpha`), tamaño fino (`markersize`) y micro-desplazamiento\\n        determinista (`jitter` con semilla fija) para evitar la superposición ciega\\n        de eventos ocurridos en una misma esquina o centroide barrial.\\n      • Salida física: `reports/figuras/mapa_diagnostico_continental.png` a `300 DPI`.\\n\\nEn palabras simples:\\n    Es la \\\"prueba visual\\\" de que las Fases 4 y 5 funcionaron bien: si alguna coordenada\\n    hubiera quedado corrupta o invertida, veríamos puntos flotando en el Océano Pacífico\\n    o en otro continente. Al ver la nube de puntos rojos ajustada con precisión sobre\\n    el territorio continental del Ecuador, validamos visualmente la calidad espacial.\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n# `f\n<truncated 16789 bytes>","Overwrite":"true","Path":"\"D:\\\\Tesis\\\\src\\\\visualizacion\\\\mapa_diagnostico.py\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
